!!! archon/rules/generic.mat
!!! Language-agnostic code and security rules.
!!!
!!! These rules describe issues that are not specific to Matrix: they apply to
!!! any source text Archon scans (C, C++, shell, configuration, and Matrix
!!! alike). They are literal patterns in this increment; later analyzers add
!!! structure and data flow without changing the finding model.

book archon.rules.generic

read everything from ny.lang.core
read everything from archon.model.severity
read everything from archon.model.confidence
read everything from archon.model.category
read everything from archon.model.rule

!!! The generic rule set, in stable order.
public generic-rules returns array of knowledge-rule begin paragraph
    variable rules as array of knowledge-rule is []

    append (build knowledge-rule with identity being "code.unsafe-copy", title being "Unbounded string copy", needle being "strcpy(", guidance being "Use a copy that respects the destination size.", level being severity.High, certainty being confidence.Likely, domain being category.Code) to rules
    append (build knowledge-rule with identity being "code.unbounded-read", title being "Unbounded input read", needle being "gets(", guidance being "Read input with an explicit bound.", level being severity.Critical, certainty being confidence.Likely, domain being category.Code) to rules
    append (build knowledge-rule with identity being "sec.hardcoded-secret", title being "Hard-coded secret", needle being "password", guidance being "Move secrets out of source into a secret store.", level being severity.Critical, certainty being confidence.Speculative, domain being category.Security) to rules
    append (build knowledge-rule with identity being "sec.hardcoded-key", title being "Hard-coded key", needle being "api_key", guidance being "Load keys from the environment or a secret store.", level being severity.High, certainty being confidence.Speculative, domain being category.Security) to rules
    append (build knowledge-rule with identity being "sec.weak-hash", title being "Weak hash", needle being "md5(", guidance being "Use a modern hash for security purposes.", level being severity.Medium, certainty being confidence.Likely, domain being category.Security) to rules
    append (build knowledge-rule with identity being "sec.command-exec", title being "Command execution", needle being "system(", guidance being "Avoid shelling out; if required, pass fixed arguments and validate input.", level being severity.High, certainty being confidence.Speculative, domain being category.Security) to rules
    append (build knowledge-rule with identity being "perm.world-writable", title being "World-writable path", needle being "chmod 777", guidance being "Grant the narrowest permission that works.", level being severity.High, certainty being confidence.Likely, domain being category.Permission) to rules

    give rules
end paragraph
